<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by an assertion failure in the `tsx_send_msg` function. The assertion `pj_assert(!"Unexpected status!");` is triggered when the function is called with `status == PJ_SUCCESS` inside a block that is intended to handle transport errors. This block is executed when `tsx->role == PJSIP_ROLE_UAC` and `tsx->transport_flag` has the `TSX_HAS_RESOLVED_SERVER` bit set.

The fuzz driver sets the `TSX_HAS_RESOLVED_SERVER` flag in `tsx->transport_flag` and then calls `pjsip_tsx_retransmit_no_state`, which in turn calls `tsx_send_msg`. The `tsx_send_msg` function is not prepared to handle a success status in this specific scenario, leading to the assertion failure.

This is a bug in the pjsip project. The `tsx_send_msg` function should not assert on a success status, even in an error-handling block. It should either handle this case gracefully or the logic leading to this call should prevent it from happening. A potential fix would be to remove the assertion or add a check to handle the `PJ_SUCCESS` case appropriately within the error handling logic.
</crash-analysis>

